    "content": "Troy University is a public university in Troy, Alabama, founded in 1887 with a total enrollment of approximately 18,333 students. Known as \"Alabama's International University,\" it offers various undergraduate and graduate programs, boasting a 93% acceptance rate and a 47% graduation rate. The university features 16 Division I athletic teams (Trojans) and has a strong focus on student leadership. Academics and Campus Life Programs: Offers over 290 degree options, including popular majors in Business, Management, Marketing, and Nursing. Structure: Known for its active, 650-acre main campus, along with campuses in Dothan, Montgomery, and Phenix City, plus numerous worldwide service sites. Student Body: Highly diverse with strong international representation, enrolling students from over 65 countries. Athletics: Competes at the NCAA Division I level (Sun Belt Conference). Key Rankings and Recognition Top Online Programs: Niche ranked TROY as the 25th Best Online College in America. Culture: Often praised for its \"friendly spirit\" and beautiful campus setting, including the Janice Hawkins Cultural Arts Park. Admissions and Cost Acceptance Rate: 93% (as of Fall 2023). Net Price: Approximately $12,504 per year. Scholarships: Various scholarships are available for new and transfer students. Other Notable Features Military Friendly: Offers specialized support for military, veteran, and family students. Study Abroad: Features a robust international study program. Alumni Network: Approximately 175,000 alumni worldwide.",
